    {
      "depth": 2,
      "text": "The plugin entry point (Lifecycle)",
      "id": "the-plugin-entry-point-lifecycle"
    },
    {
      "depth": 2,
      "text": "The MapComponent: where functionality lives",
      "id": "the-mapcomponent-where-functionality-lives"
    },
    {
      "depth": 2,
      "text": "The Tool: the toolbar button",
      "id": "the-tool-the-toolbar-button"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<p>Two of your four classes are the entry points ATAK calls: the <strong>Lifecycle</strong> (your <code>IPlugin</code>) and the <strong>Tool</strong>. The Lifecycle brings your functionality online; the Tool gives the user a button to open it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-plugin-entry-point-lifecycle\"><a href=\"#the-plugin-entry-point-lifecycle\">The plugin entry point (Lifecycle)</a></h2>\n<p>ATAK 5.x instantiates the class named in <code>plugin.xml</code> under the <code>gov.tak.api.plugin.IPlugin</code> extension. In practice you extend <code>**AbstractPlugin**</code>, whose constructor receives an <code>**IServiceController**</code> plus the components your plugin registers — its <strong>Tool</strong> (the button) and one or more <strong>MapComponents</strong>:</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "html": "<pre class=\"shiki one-dark-pro\" style=\"background-color:#282c34;color:#abb2bf\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">package</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> com.atakmap.android.helloworld.plugin</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">import</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> com.atak.plugins.impl.AbstractPlugin</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">import</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> com.atak.plugins.impl.PluginContextProvider</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">import</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> gov.tak.api.plugin.IServiceController</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">import</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> com.atakmap.android.helloworld.HelloWorldMapComponent</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> class</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> HelloWorldLifecycle</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> extends</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> AbstractPlugin</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> HelloWorldLifecycle</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">IServiceController</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> serviceController</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">        super</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(serviceController,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">                new</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> HelloWorldTool</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(serviceController</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">                        .</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getService</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">PluginContextProvider</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">class</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">                        .</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getPluginContext</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">()),</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">                new</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> HelloWorldMapComponent</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">}</span></span></code></pre>",
      "lang": "java"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<p>Two things to note:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The <code>**IServiceController**</code> is your gateway to ATAK's services. Here it provides the <strong>plugin context</strong> (via <code>PluginContextProvider</code>) needed to construct the Tool.</li>\n<li><code>AbstractPlugin</code> forwards ATAK's lifecycle callbacks to the MapComponent(s) you pass, and registers the Tool. For most plugins this class never grows beyond this — it's the single place that names the two pieces below.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-mapcomponent-where-functionality-lives\"><a href=\"#the-mapcomponent-where-functionality-lives\">The MapComponent: where functionality lives</a></h2>\n<p>The MapComponent is the real workhorse. The example extends <code>DropDownMapComponent</code> (a MapComponent that already knows how to host slide-in panels) and overrides the lifecycle hooks. The important one is <code>**onCreate**</code>, where you register your receivers and wire up the map:</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "html": "<pre class=\"shiki one-dark-pro\" style=\"background-color:#282c34;color:#abb2bf\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> class</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> HelloWorldMapComponent</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> extends</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> DropDownMapComponent</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> static</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> final</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> String</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> TAG </span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">=</span><span style=\"color:#98C379\"> \"HelloWorldMapComponent\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> Context</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> pluginContext</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> HelloWorldDropDownReceiver</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> dropDown</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Override</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> void</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> onCreate</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">final</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> Context</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">, </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Intent</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> intent</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">, </span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">final</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> MapView</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> view</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">        // The theme must be set programmatically — the plugin's own</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">        // AndroidManifest theme is NOT applied when it loads inside ATAK.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">        context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">setTheme</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">R</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">style</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">ATAKPluginTheme</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">        super</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">onCreate</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(context, intent, view);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">        pluginContext </span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">=</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> context;       </span><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// hold the plugin context for the UI layer</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">        // Create your UI receiver and register it against the action(s) it handles.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">        this</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">dropDown</span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> HelloWorldDropDownReceiver</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(view, context, mapOverlay);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">        DocumentedIntentFilter</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> ddFilter</span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> DocumentedIntentFilter</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">        ddFilter</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">addAction</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">HelloWorldDropDownReceiver</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">SHOW_HELLO_WORLD</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#98C379\">                \"Show the Hello World drop-down\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">        this</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">registerDropDownReceiver</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">this</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">dropDown</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">, ddFilter);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Override</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> void</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> onStart</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Context</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">, </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">MapView</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> view</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">  { </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Log</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">d</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(TAG, </span><span style=\"color:#98C379\">\"onStart\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">); }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Override</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> void</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> onResume</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Context</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">, </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">MapView</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> view</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> { </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Log</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">d</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(TAG, </span><span style=\"color:#98C379\">\"onResume\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">); }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Override</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> void</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> onPause</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Context</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">, </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">MapView</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> view</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">  { </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Log</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">d</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(TAG, </span><span style=\"color:#98C379\">\"onPause\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">); }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Override</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> void</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> onStop</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Context</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">, </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">MapView</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> view</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">   { </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Log</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">d</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(TAG, </span><span style=\"color:#98C379\">\"onStop\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">); }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">}</span></span></code></pre>",
      "lang": "java"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<p>Key points:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>**registerDropDownReceiver(receiver, filter)**</code> connects a <code>DropDownReceiver</code> (your UI) to a broadcast action. When that action fires, ATAK shows the panel. A MapComponent can register several receivers.</li>\n<li><code>**DocumentedIntentFilter**</code> is ATAK's self-documenting <code>IntentFilter</code> — use it instead of a raw <code>IntentFilter</code> for the actions your plugin handles.</li>\n<li>Hold on to <code>**pluginContext**</code> here; the UI layer needs it to inflate your layouts.</li>\n<li><code>DropDownMapComponent</code> provides a default <code>onDestroy</code> that unregisters what you registered through it. If you register your own broadcast receivers or add map items directly, undo that in your own <code>onDestroy</code>/cleanup.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-tool-the-toolbar-button\"><a href=\"#the-tool-the-toolbar-button\">The Tool: the toolbar button</a></h2>\n<p>The Tool is the <code>HelloWorldTool</code> you passed to <code>AbstractPlugin</code> above. (In ATAK 4.x this was a separate <code>plugin.xml</code> <code>ToolDescriptor</code> extension; in 5.x the entry point registers it for you.) Extending <code>AbstractPluginTool</code> gives ATAK a button in the toolbar / navigation that, when tapped, <strong>broadcasts the action that opens your DropDown</strong> — closing the loop with the receiver you registered in the MapComponent:</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "html": "<pre class=\"shiki one-dark-pro\" style=\"background-color:#282c34;color:#abb2bf\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> class</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> HelloWorldTool</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> extends</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> AbstractPluginTool</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> implements</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> Disposable</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> HelloWorldTool</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">final</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> Context</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">        super</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(context,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">                context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getString</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">R</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">string</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">app_name</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">),               </span><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// label</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">                context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getString</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">R</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">string</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">app_name</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">),               </span><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// description</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">                context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getResources</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">().</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getDrawable</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">R</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">drawable</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">ic_launcher</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">), </span><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// icon</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#98C379\">                \"com.atakmap.android.helloworld.SHOW_HELLO_WORLD\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">);  </span><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// action to fire</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Override</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> void</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> dispose</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">()</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> { </span><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">/* unregister anything you registered */</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">}</span></span></code></pre>",
      "lang": "java"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<p>The fourth constructor argument is the same action string your <code>DropDownReceiver</code> listens for. That's the entire path: <strong>user taps the tool button → ATAK broadcasts</strong> <code>**SHOW_HELLO_WORLD**</code> <strong>→ your registered</strong> <code>**DropDownReceiver**</code> <strong>shows its panel.</strong></p>\n<p><code>AbstractPluginTool</code> also lets you decorate the button — for example the example increments a numeric <strong>badge count</strong> on the button via <code>NavButtonManager</code> in response to its own broadcast. That's optional polish, not required wiring.</p>\n<p>→ Next: <a href=\"/en/working-with-tak/build-a-ui-the-dropdown-panel-kaH71FJeG8\">Build a UI: the DropDown panel</a>.</p>"
    }
  ]
}
